{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MjZpmgmeEBBzJ4Db2XjYHn","type":"tool_result","content":"335\t**Summary**: Swept 10 parameter configurations via environment variables. Raising MIN_N (shifting layers from PrecomputeM to FoldEval) made GKR monotonically worse: MIN_N=24 +6ms, MIN_N=26 +24ms, MIN_N=28 +68ms, disabled +87ms. Lowering MIN_N (more PrecomputeM layers) had no measurable benefit: MIN_N=20 -2ms, MIN_N=18 -4ms, MIN_N=16 +19ms. TARGET_BLOCKS and TAIL_TILE sweeps were also within noise (±14ms). The current defaults are near-optimal. Key finding: PrecomputeM is faster than FoldEval for layers at rem_n≥22 because its windowed approach (w=3) amortizes per-round D2H sync + CPU transcript overhead, saving ~2-3ms per window vs 3 FoldEval rounds. Fixed a buffer sizing bug where the work buffer used the compile-time MIN_N constant instead of the runtime env var value, causing CUDA crashes when MIN_N is overridden to a higher value.\n336\t\n337\t## 2026-04-16-1430-column-batched-ntt-for-rs-code-matrix\n338\t\n339\t**Idea**: Split the forward NTT in rs_code_matrix into L2-cache-sized column batches (~1000 columns, ~64MB per batch) to improve memory locality for the 3.4GB working set at APC 300."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fca59fa0-eca1-4639-8acf-142eae8eef60","uuid":"cee50c8f-fcb1-437a-ba22-e2bbe926c017","timestamp":"2026-04-16T14:51:02.730Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/log.md","content":"**Summary**: Swept 10 parameter configurations via environment variables. Raising MIN_N (shifting layers from PrecomputeM to FoldEval) made GKR monotonically worse: MIN_N=24 +6ms, MIN_N=26 +24ms, MIN_N=28 +68ms, disabled +87ms. Lowering MIN_N (more PrecomputeM layers) had no measurable benefit: MIN_N=20 -2ms, MIN_N=18 -4ms, MIN_N=16 +19ms. TARGET_BLOCKS and TAIL_TILE sweeps were also within noise (±14ms). The current defaults are near-optimal. Key finding: PrecomputeM is faster than FoldEval for layers at rem_n≥22 because its windowed approach (w=3) amortizes per-round D2H sync + CPU transcript overhead, saving ~2-3ms per window vs 3 FoldEval rounds. Fixed a buffer sizing bug where the work buffer used the compile-time MIN_N constant instead of the runtime env var value, causing CUDA crashes when MIN_N is overridden to a higher value.\n\n## 2026-04-16-1430-column-batched-ntt-for-rs-code-matrix\n\n**Idea**: Split the forward NTT in rs_code_matrix into L2-cache-sized column batches (~1000 columns, ~64MB per batch) to improve memory locality for the 3.4GB working set at APC 300.","numLines":5,"startLine":335,"totalLines":344}}}
